DESCRIPTION:AppDev SIG Presents:\nRolling Your own Replication\nSpeaker: Br
	ent Ozar\nMay 19th 1:00pm ET\nTopic Description: SQL Server's built-in rep
	lication has made great strides in the last couple of versions\, but what 
	if it's still not enough?  One team needed more flexibility\, easier admin
	istration and higher scalability\, so they built their own solution instea
	d.  Brent Ozar will discuss how the system was architected\, the pros and 
	cons\, and how you can build a similar solution for your own needs.  He'll
	 explain some of the lessons learned in scaling this out to thousands of r
	emote SQL Servers.\n\n\nNotes  \nBlythe Morrow has invited you to attend a
	n online meeting using Live Meeting. Join the meeting. <https://owa.sqlpas
	s.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3a%2f%2fwww.livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fusergrou
	ps%2fjoin%3fid%3d35G2MC%26role%3dattend>  \n\nAudio Information \nTelephon
	e conferencing\nUse the information below to connect: \nToll-free: +1 (866
	) 379-8990 \nParticipant code: 6489756 \nFirst Time Users: \nTo save time 
	before the meeting\, check your system  <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir
	.aspx?URL=http%3a%2f%2fgo.microsoft.com%2ffwlink%2f%3fLinkId%3d90703> to m
	ake sure it is ready to use Microsoft Office Live Meeting. \nTroubleshooti
	ng\nUnable to join the meeting? Follow these steps: \n1.	Copy this address
	 and paste it into your web browser: \nhttps://www.livemeeting.com/cc/user
	groups/join <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3a%2f%2fwww.
	livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fusergroups%2fjoin>  \n2.	Copy and paste the require
	d information: \nMeeting ID: 35G2MC \nLocation: https://www.livemeeting.co
	m/cc/usergroups <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=https%3a%2f%2f
	www.livemeeting.com%2fcc%2fusergroups>  \nIf you still cannot enter the me
	eting\, contact support <https://owa.sqlpass.org/owa/redir.aspx?URL=http%3
	a%2f%2fr.office.microsoft.com%2fr%2frlidLiveMeeting%3fp1%3d12%26p2%3den_US
	%26p3%3dLMInfo%26p4%3dsupport> \n\nNotice \nMicrosoft Office Live Meeting 
	can be used to record meetings. By participating in this meeting\, you agr
	ee that your communications may be monitored or recorded at any time durin
	g the meeting. \n\n
